.TH IMPROVE 1 "" "Improve 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
improve \- deterministic Ada quality remediation planning
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B improve
command [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Improve reads completed Ada Quality assessments, stores immutable remediation plans, and publishes approved work as
native model_runner tasks.
.SH COMMANDS
projects, findings, plan, audit, apply, tasks, status, refresh, verify, recover, doctor, config, completion, manpage,
help, and version.
.SH PLAN OPERATIONS
plan supports list, show, approve, diff, and explain in addition to deterministic generation.
.SH AUDIT
audit PLAN-ID [--revision N] exports immutable provenance, approval, publication, and verification evidence.
.SH OUTPUT
--format accepts terminal, json, or markdown. JSON output and JSON errors are single versioned documents.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 unresolved verification or unhealthy diagnostics; 2 invalid input; 3 unavailable evidence; 4 storage or
internal failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
ada_quality(1), model_runner(1)
